    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Born into slavery around 1730 of African and Native American parentage, Crispus Attucks escaped to become a sailor and a leading voice for American liberty in Boston, dying (and being Embraced on the spot by Marguerite Foccart) at the 1770 Boston Massacre. He fought the Redcoats, ran the Underground Railroad, and battled Ventrue and Toreador plantation-owners through the Civil War era before traveling west to help Jeremy MacNeil overthrow Don Sebastian in 1944. He now serves the Free States as Jeremy's most trusted enforcer and \"muscle.\"</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Quiet dignity backed by real menace. You have fought for freedom for two and a half centuries and do not take kindly to being dismissed as merely muscle.</p>",
    "notes": "Jeremy MacNeil's most trusted enforcer. Respected by leadership, underestimated by rank-and-file anarchs as 'one of MacNeil's boys.'",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
